# Golden characterization files are compared byte-for-byte against strings the
# Go program emits at runtime, and the runtime always writes LF. On a checkout
# with core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) the working-tree copies would
# otherwise be converted to CRLF, making TestCharacterization_HelpGolden fail
# for a reason unrelated to any code change. Pin the goldens to LF in every
# working tree so the comparison is platform-independent.
testdata/*.golden eol=lf
